   "source": [
    "# Koordinates Statistical Area lookup notebook\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is intended to be run to add statistical areas to the AirBnB dataset prepared earlier, via querying the Koordinates service.\n",
    "\n",
    "The API query is wrapped up in a function that can be parallelised to several workers. You can set the number of workers in the cell below (after imports). You will also need to prepare your Koordinates key and place it within an .env file in the project root directory with api_key = KEY\n",
    "\n",
    "WARNING: do not run this unless you absolutely have to! The API queries will take quite a while to run, so make sure you store the results and rerun this notebook sparingly!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "1309da580c3d0c7",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-09-19T00:02:06.984688500Z",
     "start_time": "2026-09-19T00:02:06.974090400Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Imports\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from dotenv import load_dotenv\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import requests\n",
    "from concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "86354f8f42aa8818",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-09-19T00:02:07.084635800Z",
     "start_time": "2026-09-19T00:02:06.986894600Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Config cell + loading secrets/data\n",
    "# Parameters: file paths, number of workers and the Koordinates layer/URL can be changed here\n",
    "INPUT_PATH = \"cleaned_chch_airbnb.csv\"\n",
    "OUTPUT_PATH = \"sa_aug_cleaned_chch_airbnb.csv\"\n",
    "NUM_WORKERS = 8\n",
    "SA2_LAYER_ID = 98970 # This is the SA2 layer for Stats NZ\n",
    "KOORDINATES_URL = \"https://koordinates.com/services/query/v1/vector.json\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get prepared Chch AirBnB data\n",
    "airbnb_data = pd.read_csv(INPUT_PATH)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get Koordinates API key\n",
    "load_dotenv()\n",
    "api_key = os.getenv(\"api_key\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a2d33acf4b5ec7e5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## API query\n",
    "\n",
    "The function below is used by the individual workers later to query the Koordinates service. It is able to take a lat/long pair, query the layer of interest at Koordinates, and return the SA code for that specific GPS coordinate."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 31,
   "id": "4d1f06cbd4215684",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-09-19T00:13:41.202604500Z",
     "start_time": "2026-09-19T00:13:41.187747800Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Defining the function used for queries run by workers\n",
    "# Takes latitude and longitude as inputs and returns the SA2 code,\n",
    "# or None if the lookup fails (so one bad point doesn't stop the whole run\n",
    "# and failures show up in the NA check below)\n",
    "def koord_query(lat, lon):\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Setting up parameters for API query, like which layer and the coordinates of the AirBnB we want to query\n",
    "    parameters = {\n",
    "        \"key\": api_key,\n",
    "        \"layer\": SA2_LAYER_ID,\n",
    "        \"x\": lon,\n",
    "        \"y\": lat\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        # Setting up API call + returning status and data as json\n",
    "        response = requests.get(\"https://koordinates.com/services/query/v1/vector.json\",\n",
    "# Setting up API call + returning status and data as json\n",
    "# If the request fails, or the point isn't inside any SA2, return None so the NA check can catch it\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        response = requests.get(KOORDINATES_URL,\n",
    "                                params = parameters,\n",
    "                                timeout = 10)\n",
    "\n",
    "        response.raise_for_status()\n",
    "        data = response.json()\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Returning just the SA22019_V1_00 from the json\n",
    "        return data[\"vectorQuery\"][\"layers\"][\"98970\"][\"features\"][0][\"properties\"][\"SA22019_V1_00\"]\n",
    "    except (requests.RequestException, ValueError, KeyError, IndexError):\n",
    "# Returning just the SA22019_V1_00 from the json\n",
    "        return(data[\"vectorQuery\"][\"layers\"][str(SA2_LAYER_ID)][\"features\"][0][\"properties\"][\"SA22019_V1_00\"])\n",
    "    except (requests.RequestException, KeyError, IndexError, ValueError):\n",
    "        return None"
   ]
  },
